# Shell scripts keep LF endings whatever platform they are edited on.
# A CRLF here is not cosmetic: `#!/usr/bin/env bash\r` makes the kernel look
# for an interpreter named "bash\r", and the container or the timer dies at
# startup with "no such file or directory" pointing at a file that plainly
# exists. These are edited on Windows and run on Linux, which is the path that
# trips it.
*.sh text eol=lf
